# The CI guards are Bash, and they run from the working tree — so on a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true they were checked out CRLF and `bash` failed
# to parse `set -uo pipefail` before reaching a single check. CI never saw it:
# its Linux checkout is LF either way, so the scripts were green in the one
# place they could not catch a local mistake, and unrunnable in the one place
# they could.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for everything Ansible parses or ships to a Debian host:
# templates render into files a Linux service reads, and a stray CR is a
# configuration bug that only appears on the node.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.j2 text eol=lf
*.cfg text eol=lf
